+## Implementation and tests
+
+- Follow surrounding formatting; document environment/configuration knobs in `readme-dev.md`.
+- Managed-profile tokens identify independent uses, never exclusive leases. Write only
+  matching host-owned proofs; remove tokens from child env. Never restrict concurrent
+  profile use or refresh credentials. Classify refresh failures on new/resume/fork/load;
+  mark only reused-token contention, without logout. Legacy load keeps its error path.
+- Every console child spawn sets `windowsHide: true`; `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE` is separate.
+- Use null for a completed lookup with no result, undefined for optional parameters,
+  and the surrounding state convention. Incoming optional null means absent.
+- Handle every union/event switch variant explicitly, including no-op cases.
+  Never add a fallback just to satisfy TypeScript. Keep comments concise and concrete.
+- Read the owning module before coding. Extend existing mechanisms and put shared rules
+  with their owner. Reuse rules across live/history and sibling handlers; avoid parallel
+  fallbacks. Explain unavoidable provider workarounds in code and the PR.
+- Preserve ACP v1/v2 behavior. v2 converts to v1 and reuses its logic; keep v2 differences
+  in conversion. New optional fields and metadata must accept previously valid requests.
+- Tests live in `src/__tests__/`. Use event-driven observable behavior and snapshots
+  (`toMatchFileSnapshot`). Stabilize drifting payloads except model/list.
+- Cover client-visible changes on both protocol versions; internal-only tests need no
+  duplication. Search existing coverage; combine equivalent inputs with `it.each`.
+  Every documented behavior needs a regression test. Wire tests must add boundary coverage.
+- Use `/run-codex` (`.claude/skills/run-codex/`) for authorized real-provider tests.
 
